D("salt-tolerant",{etymology:E("A compound of salt + tolerant; tolerant comes through French from Latin tolerant- ‘enduring’, from tolerare ‘bear’.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/tolerant"),contexts:[C("salt-tolerant.s1","農業","The coastal farmer chose a salt-tolerant bean because its roots could survive the brackish irrigation water.","沿海农户选择了耐盐豆类，因为它的根能在微咸的灌溉水中存活。","Salt-tolerant describes a plant able to survive high salt concentration.","Because introduces the condition that makes the variety suitable.","This is resistance to salt stress, not a salty taste.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The salt-tolerant seedlings died as soon as a trace of salt touched their roots, showing that they could not endure salt.","The salt-sensitive seedlings died when salt reached their roots; salt-tolerant seedlings can survive higher salt levels.","Salt-tolerant means able to withstand salt; immediate harm from a trace shows sensitivity instead.")],quiz:[Q("salt-tolerant.q1","salt-tolerant.s1","meaning","A salt-tolerant crop is one that ___.",["can survive relatively salty conditions","must grow only in fresh water","tastes strongly of salt"],"can survive relatively salty conditions","Tolerant describes survival despite salt exposure.","meaning"),Q("salt-tolerant.q2","salt-tolerant.s1","context","Which plant would be called salt-tolerant?",["A bean that grows in brackish soil","A fern that dies in salty soil","A plant whose leaves taste sweet"],"A bean that grows in brackish soil","The plant survives salt in its environment.","context"),Q("salt-tolerant.q3","salt-tolerant.s1","word-formation","In salt-tolerant, tolerant means able to ___.",["endure a condition","make salt","remove a root"],"endure a condition","The compound names ability to withstand salt.","word-formation"),Q("salt-tolerant.q4","salt-tolerant.s1","meaning","Salt-tolerant is closest in meaning to ___.",["able to withstand salt","containing no water","used to season food"],"able to withstand salt","The adjective describes resistance to a salty environment.","meaning")]});
D("saltiness",{etymology:E("From salty + -ness, the noun-forming suffix; salty derives from salt, an Old English word of Germanic origin.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/salty"),contexts:[C("saltiness.s1","烹飪","The cook tasted the broth before adding soy sauce because the smoked fish had already increased its saltiness.","厨师在加酱油前先尝了汤，因为烟熏鱼已经使咸味变重。","Saltiness is the degree to which food tastes of salt.","Because explains the caution; its refers to the broth's taste.","The noun names the perceived salty flavor.")],mistakes:[M("word form","The saltiness of these olives are too strong for the salad.","The saltiness of these olives is too strong for the salad.","Saltiness is a singular abstract noun and takes is.")],quiz:[Q("saltiness.q1","saltiness.s1","meaning","A high saltiness level means food tastes ___.",["strongly of salt","strongly of sugar","free of all flavor"],"strongly of salt","Saltiness names the degree of salty taste.","meaning"),Q("saltiness.q2","saltiness.s1","context","A cook adds lemon after tasting the soup's saltiness to ___.",["balance its salty taste","make it a salt-tolerant plant","turn it into a saucer"],"balance its salty taste","The cook adjusts the flavor after tasting salt.","context"),Q("saltiness.q3","saltiness.s1","word-formation","The suffix -ness in saltiness makes ___.",["a noun for a quality","a past-tense verb","an adverb"],"a noun for a quality","-ness turns the adjective salty into the quality noun saltiness.","word-formation"),Q("saltiness.q4","saltiness.s1","meaning","Which phrase describes saltiness?",["the salty taste of the cheese","the cheese's blue color","the cheese's price"],"the salty taste of the cheese","Saltiness concerns how strongly something tastes of salt.","meaning")]});
D("saltwater",{etymology:E("A compound of salt + water; the adjective describes water that contains salt, especially seawater, and organisms living in it.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/saltwater"),contexts:[C("saltwater.s1","海洋","The saltwater aquarium needs a filter that can keep the marine plants healthy.","咸水水族箱需要一台能保持海洋植物健康的过滤器。","Saltwater means of or living in salty water such as the sea.","That can keep describes the filter's function; marine plants establish the setting.","The adjective classifies the aquarium by water type.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","A saltwater aquarium is filled with fresh water from a mountain stream and has no added salt.","A freshwater aquarium is filled with fresh water from a mountain stream and has no added salt.","Saltwater describes salty water; a fresh stream is freshwater.")],quiz:[Q("saltwater.q1","saltwater.s1","meaning","A saltwater fish normally lives in ___.",["the sea or other salty water","a dry desert","a freshwater pond only"],"the sea or other salty water","The adjective identifies a saline habitat.","meaning"),Q("saltwater.q2","saltwater.s1","context","Which setup is a saltwater aquarium?",["A tank modeled on a coral reef","A tank of rainwater with trout","A dry glass display case"],"A tank modeled on a coral reef","Coral reef organisms live in saltwater.","context"),Q("saltwater.q3","saltwater.s1","word-choice","The ____ marsh flooded with seawater at high tide.",["saltwater","saltiness","salutary"],"saltwater","Saltwater modifies a habitat containing salty water.","word-choice"),Q("saltwater.q4","saltwater.s1","meaning","In saltwater plants, saltwater tells you ___.",["the type of water where they live","their exact height","how sweet their leaves taste"],"the type of water where they live","It describes their saline environment.","meaning")]});
D("salty",{etymology:E("From salt + adjective-forming -y; salt is an Old English word of Germanic origin, from Proto-Germanic *saltom.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/salty"),contexts:[C("salty.s1","飲食","The olives made the pasta sauce too salty, so Lena added tomatoes rather than more cheese.","橄榄让意面酱太咸了，所以 Lena 加了番茄而不是更多奶酪。","Salty means containing or tasting strongly of salt.","Too modifies salty; so gives Lena's corrective action.","This is the taste sense.") ,C("salty.s2","言談","The comedian's salty jokes made the adults laugh, but the host left them out of the family broadcast.","喜剧演员略带粗俗的笑话逗笑了成年人，但主持人没有把它们放进家庭广播。","Salty can describe remarks that are sharp, lively, and slightly indecent.","But contrasts adult amusement with the host's audience decision.","This is the informal language sense, not food flavor.")],mistakes:[M("register","The host used a salty joke in a children's broadcast, although its wording was mildly indecent.","The host replaced the salty joke with a clean one before the children's broadcast.","Salty can describe slightly indecent remarks; that register is unsuitable for a children's broadcast.")],quiz:[Q("salty.q1","salty.s1","meaning","A salty soup tastes ___.",["of too much salt","like plain water","of sweet fruit"],"of too much salt","This is the food-flavor sense.","meaning"),Q("salty.q2","salty.s2","context","A salty remark at a formal family event is likely ___.",["sharp and mildly indecent","about the salt content of soup","a respectful military gesture"],"sharp and mildly indecent","The figurative sense describes lively, sometimes coarse language.","context"),Q("salty.q3","salty.s1","collocation","The chef added water because the stew was too ____.",["salty","sanctimonious","sane"],"salty","Too salty describes excess salt flavor.","collocation"),Q("salty.q4","salty.s2","register","Which is a suitable description of salty humor?",["lively and somewhat coarse","quietly reverent","a type of seawater"],"lively and somewhat coarse","The informal figurative sense applies to sharp, slightly indecent remarks.","register")]});
D("salutary",{etymology:E("From Latin salutaris ‘healthful, beneficial’, from salus ‘health, safety’; English uses it for an effect that improves matters, often by teaching a lesson.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/salutary"),contexts:[C("salutary.s1","政策","The costly blackout had a salutary effect: the hospital installed backup power before the next storm.","那次代价高昂的停电起到了有益的警示作用：医院在下一场风暴前安装了备用电源。","Salutary means producing a beneficial effect, especially a warning one.","Colon introduces the practical improvement; before sets its timing.","The bad event prompts a useful preventive change.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The salutary warning had no useful effect, taught nobody anything, and led the hospital to remove its backup generator.","The salutary warning led the hospital to install a backup generator before another blackout.","Salutary means beneficial; an ignored warning that worsens preparedness is not salutary.")],quiz:[Q("salutary.q1","salutary.s1","meaning","A salutary lesson is one that ___.",["has a beneficial effect or teaches a useful warning","makes a problem worse","describes a salty taste"],"has a beneficial effect or teaches a useful warning","Salutary means beneficial, often because it warns.","meaning"),Q("salutary.q2","salutary.s1","context","A minor accident leads a factory to improve safety checks. The accident had a ____ effect.",["salutary","sardonic","saltwater"],"salutary","The event produced a useful preventive improvement.","context"),Q("salutary.q3","salutary.s1","collocation","The audit had a ____ effect on the firm's record-keeping.",["salutary","same here","salver"],"salutary","A salutary effect is a helpful result.","collocation"),Q("salutary.q4","salutary.s1","meaning","Which outcome is salutary?",["A warning prompts effective safety improvements.","A warning is ignored and conditions worsen.","A warning adds salt to a recipe."],"A warning prompts effective safety improvements.","The warning produces a beneficial change.","meaning")]});
D("salute",{etymology:E("From Italian salutare and Latin salutare ‘wish health, greet’, from salus ‘health’; English uses it for a formal gesture and for public praise.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/salute"),contexts:[C("salute.s1","軍事","The cadets gave a salute as the flag was raised at the ceremony.","仪式上升旗时，学员们行礼致敬。","A salute is a gesture of respect, often raising a hand to the head.","As the flag was raised gives the occasion for the gesture.","This is the noun for the gesture.") ,C("salute.s2","軍事","The guard saluted the visiting officer before opening the gate.","卫兵在打开大门前向来访军官行礼。","To salute someone is to make a formal gesture of respect.","The officer is the direct object; before marks the timing.","This is the verb for performing the gesture.") ,C("salute.s3","公共生活","The newspaper saluted the volunteers for keeping the shelter open through the storm.","报纸公开赞扬了志愿者在风暴期间坚持开放避难所。","Salute can mean praise or show public respect.","For introduces what is praised; through states their effort.","This is figurative public praise.")],mistakes:[M("word form","The guards salutes the officer as she entered the hall.","The guards salute the officer as she entered the hall.","The plural subject guards takes the base verb salute.")],quiz:[Q("salute.q1","salute.s1","meaning","A military salute is ___.",["a formal gesture of respect","a tray for carrying cups","a warning about a storm"],"a formal gesture of respect","The noun sense is a respectful gesture.","meaning"),Q("salute.q2","salute.s2","context","A soldier salutes a commander by ___.",["making a formal gesture of respect","selling supplies to the public","saving goods from a flood"],"making a formal gesture of respect","The verb names the action of the gesture.","context"),Q("salute.q3","salute.s3","meaning","A newspaper salutes a volunteer when it ___.",["publicly praises the volunteer","orders the volunteer to leave","measures the volunteer's height"],"publicly praises the volunteer","This is the figurative praise sense.","meaning"),Q("salute.q4","salute.s2","grammar","Choose the correct sentence.",["The guard saluted the officer.","The guard saluted to the officer.","The guard was salute the officer."],"The guard saluted the officer.","Salute takes the person as a direct object.","grammar")]});
D("salvage",{etymology:E("From French salvage, related to salver ‘save’, ultimately Latin salvare ‘make safe’; it names goods saved from disaster and the act of saving them.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/salvage"),contexts:[C("salvage.s1","海難","The crew sorted the salvage from the wreck, setting aside intact tools and sealed food tins.","船员整理了沉船中抢救出的物品，把完好的工具和密封食品罐放在一边。","Salvage as a noun is goods saved from a fire, wreck, or flood.","From the wreck identifies the source; setting aside describes sorting.","These goods survived the disaster and were recovered.") ,C("salvage.s2","工程","Engineers salvaged the bridge's steel beams after the flood so they could be reused in a safer design.","洪水过后，工程师抢救了桥上的钢梁，以便在更安全的设计中重新使用。","Salvage as a verb means save something from destruction or waste.","After the flood gives the circumstance; so states the reuse purpose.","The beams are recovered rather than discarded.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The crew called burned, unusable debris salvage even though nothing had been recovered or saved from the wreck.","The crew called the intact tools recovered from the wreck salvage.","Salvage is material saved from a disaster; irrecoverable debris has not been salvaged.")],quiz:[Q("salvage.q1","salvage.s1","meaning","Salvage from a shipwreck is ___.",["goods recovered from the wreck","a salute to the crew","the ship's original ticket"],"goods recovered from the wreck","The noun names goods saved from a wreck.","meaning"),Q("salvage.q2","salvage.s2","context","Workers salvage bricks from a ruined wall when they ___.",["recover them for safe reuse","throw every brick away","paint the wall a new color"],"recover them for safe reuse","The verb means save something from waste or destruction.","context"),Q("salvage.q3","salvage.s2","collocation","The team tried to ____ what it could from the flooded archive.",["salvage","sanctimonious","sameness"],"salvage","Salvage what can be recovered is a natural construction.","collocation"),Q("salvage.q4","salvage.s1","meaning","Which item is salvage?",["An intact radio recovered from a wreck","A newly purchased radio in a shop","A radio destroyed beyond use"],"An intact radio recovered from a wreck","Salvage consists of goods saved from disaster.","meaning")]});
D("salvation",{etymology:E("From Old French salvacion and Latin salvationem, from salvare ‘save’; it names deliverance from sin in Christian belief and, figuratively, a means of avoiding failure or trouble.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/salvation"),contexts:[C("salvation.s1","宗教","The hymn describes salvation as release from sin and a restored relationship with God.","这首圣歌把救赎描述为脱离罪并恢复与上帝的关系。","In Christian belief salvation is being saved from sin and its results.","As introduces the description; and joins the two aspects.","This is the religious sense.") ,C("salvation.s2","日常","The spare battery was our salvation when the storm cut power during the night shift.","夜班时风暴切断电力，备用电池救了急。","Salvation can figuratively mean something that prevents failure or great trouble.","When gives the crisis; the battery's role is the solution.","The noun is used figuratively for a timely rescue.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The spare battery was no salvation because it failed before the power went out and could not help the team.","The spare battery was our salvation because it kept the emergency radio working during the outage.","Salvation figuratively means something that prevents serious trouble; a useless battery cannot do so.")],quiz:[Q("salvation.q1","salvation.s1","meaning","In Christian belief, salvation concerns being saved from ___.",["sin and its results","saltwater","a public survey"],"sin and its results","This is the religious sense.","meaning"),Q("salvation.q2","salvation.s2","context","A working generator was the crew's salvation during the blackout because it ___.",["prevented the emergency from becoming worse","caused the power to fail","made the crew retire"],"prevented the emergency from becoming worse","This is the figurative rescue sense.","context"),Q("salvation.q3","salvation.s2","meaning","Which sentence uses salvation figuratively?",["The spare key was our salvation when the lock jammed.","The sermon discussed salvation from sin.","The salver held the cups."],"The spare key was our salvation when the lock jammed.","The key prevents a practical problem.","meaning"),Q("salvation.q4","salvation.s1","context","A hymn about salvation is most likely addressing ___.",["religious deliverance from sin","recovered goods from a wreck","a tray for serving letters"],"religious deliverance from sin","This is the Christian-belief sense.","context")]});
D("salver",{etymology:E("From Spanish salva ‘a tray for serving’, related to salvar ‘save’; English adopted the word for a flat tray used to carry and present food, drink, or letters.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/salver"),contexts:[C("salver.s1","服務","The attendant carried the sealed invitation on a silver salver and offered it to the guest.","侍者把密封的邀请函放在银托盘上，递给客人。","A salver is a flat tray used to carry and offer food, drinks, or letters.","On the salver describes where the invitation rests; and coordinates actions.","The tray presents an item to someone.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The attendant wore a salver on one foot while walking across the room.","The attendant carried the invitation on a salver while walking across the room.","A salver is a flat serving tray, not footwear.")],quiz:[Q("salver.q1","salver.s1","meaning","A salver is ___.",["a flat tray for carrying and offering items","a salt-tolerant plant","a formal hand gesture"],"a flat tray for carrying and offering items","The noun names a serving tray.","meaning"),Q("salver.q2","salver.s1","context","A butler brings tea on a salver. The salver is ___.",["the tray carrying the tea","the cup's handle","the room where tea is grown"],"the tray carrying the tea","It holds and presents items.","context"),Q("salver.q3","salver.s1","collocation","The letters arrived on a polished silver ____.",["salver","salute","salvation"],"salver","A salver is used to carry and offer letters.","collocation"),Q("salver.q4","salver.s1","meaning","Which item could be placed on a salver?",["A glass of water","A pair of shoes being worn","A whole dining room"],"A glass of water","A salver is a tray that carries objects.","meaning")]});
D("same",{etymology:E("From Old English same, of Germanic origin and related to words in other Germanic languages; it marks identity, the identical item, or an identical manner.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/same"),contexts:[C("same.s1","比較","We stayed in the same hotel as the survey team, but on a different floor.","我们和调查组住在同一家酒店，但在不同楼层。","Same as an adjective means not different from another person or thing.","As the survey team identifies the comparison; but contrasts the floor.","The hotel is identical, though the rooms differ.") ,C("same.s2","對話","When asked which key opened the cabinet, Niko pointed to the same as before.","有人问哪把钥匙能开柜子时，Niko 指了之前那一把。","Same can stand as a pronoun for the identical thing already mentioned.","The as before phrase identifies the prior referent.","It replaces a repeated noun such as key.") ,C("same.s3","方式","The clockmaker repaired both clocks the same, resetting each gear to its original position.","钟表匠用相同方式修好了两只钟，把每个齿轮都调回原位。","Same as an adverb means in an identical way.","The same follows repaired to describe the method; the participial phrase adds one detail.","This sense describes manner, though the sentence is formal.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","The same of the two parcels were delivered to each address.","The same parcel was delivered to each address.","Same does not take of in this construction; parcel is singular and needs was.")],quiz:[Q("same.q1","same.s1","meaning","They wore the same coat means the coat was ___.",["identical for both people","a different color for each","made of saltwater"],"identical for both people","Same as an adjective marks identity.","meaning"),Q("same.q2","same.s2","context","Asked which route she chose, Mira said 'the same as yesterday.' She chose ___.",["the identical route she chose yesterday","a new route in another town","a salty dish"],"the identical route she chose yesterday","Here same stands for the previously mentioned route.","context"),Q("same.q3","same.s1","collocation","Both teams arrived at the ____ time.",["same","salver","salutary"],"same","At the same time is the standard phrase.","collocation"),Q("same.q4","same.s3","meaning","If two devices work the same, they work ___.",["in an identical way","at different speeds by definition","only in saltwater"],"in an identical way","The adverbial sense describes manner.","meaning")]});
D("same here",{etymology:E("An informal conversational phrase combining same + here, with here locating the speaker in the same situation or response as the previous speaker.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/same"),contexts:[C("same here.s1","對話","“I am exhausted after the overnight shift.” “Same here,” said Noor, putting her bag down.","“上完夜班我累坏了。”“我也是。”Noor 说着放下包。","Same here is a reply meaning the speaker shares the feeling or situation just mentioned.","The quoted phrase echoes the preceding statement; said Noor identifies the speaker.","The phrase is a concise conversational agreement.") ,C("same here.s2","對話","“You forgot to attach the file.” “Same here,” the editor replied, admitting that she had made the same mistake.","“你忘了附文件。”“你也一样。”编辑回答，承认自己犯了同样的错误。","Same here can answer criticism by pointing out that it applies to the speaker too.","Admitting clarifies that the speaker accepts the criticism rather than denying it.","This is a reciprocal response to a criticism.")],mistakes:[M("context","After a colleague says 'I feel nervous,' Ken replies 'Same here' even though he is calm and feels no anxiety.","After a colleague says 'I feel nervous,' Ken replies 'I feel confident' if he has no anxiety.","Same here claims the speaker shares the stated feeling or situation; it is inaccurate when he does not.")],quiz:[Q("same here.q1","same here.s1","meaning","If a friend says 'I am hungry' and you reply 'Same here,' you mean ___.",["you are hungry too","you have already eaten","you are talking about a different person"],"you are hungry too","The phrase says the speaker shares the situation.","meaning"),Q("same here.q2","same here.s2","context","A colleague says, 'You missed the deadline.' You reply 'Same here' to admit that ___.",["you missed it too","the deadline was met","you never received a deadline"],"you missed it too","This use points the criticism back at the speaker as well.","context"),Q("same here.q3","same here.s1","register","Same here is most natural in ___.",["an informal conversation","a formal legal contract","a scientific measurement label"],"an informal conversation","It is a casual conversational response.","register"),Q("same here.q4","same here.s1","meaning","Which reply means the speaker shares the other person's feeling?",["'I am cold.' — 'Same here.'","'I am cold.' — 'Not me; I am warm.'","'I am cold.' — 'What time is it?'"],"'I am cold.' — 'Same here.'","The speaker reports the same condition.","meaning")]});
D("sameness",{etymology:E("From same + -ness, the suffix forming a noun for a state or quality; same is an Old English word of Germanic origin.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sameness"),contexts:[C("sameness.s1","設計","The reviewer complained that the sameness of the chapter openings made the whole guide feel repetitive.","审稿人抱怨各章开头过于雷同，使整本指南显得重复。","Sameness can mean excessive similarity with little change or variety.","That-clause states the consequence of repetitive openings.","Here the noun carries a negative sense of monotony.") ,C("sameness.s2","法律","The contract requires sameness in the dimensions of every replacement panel.","合同要求每块替换面板的尺寸完全一致。","Sameness can formally mean identity in every detail.","In the dimensions specifies the feature that must match exactly.","This is the exact-identity sense.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The report praised the sameness of the daily schedule because every day was varied and unpredictable.","The report praised the variety of the daily schedule because every day was varied and unpredictable.","Sameness means similarity or lack of variation; a varied schedule shows variety.")],quiz:[Q("sameness.q1","sameness.s1","meaning","A complaint about the sameness of a film series usually means it is ___.",["too similar and repetitive","different in every scene","made from saltwater"],"too similar and repetitive","This is the lack-of-variety sense.","meaning"),Q("sameness.q2","sameness.s2","context","A specification demands sameness in the width of all parts. Each part must have ___.",["identical width","a different color","a unique price"],"identical width","The formal sense is identity in a particular detail.","context"),Q("sameness.q3","sameness.s1","word-formation","The ending -ness in sameness creates ___.",["a noun naming a state or quality","a verb meaning to measure","a plural adjective"],"a noun naming a state or quality","-ness makes a noun from the adjective same.","word-formation"),Q("sameness.q4","sameness.s1","meaning","Which setting best illustrates monotonous sameness?",["Every chapter begins with the identical paragraph.","Each chapter uses a distinct style and structure.","The chapters cover unrelated topics."],"Every chapter begins with the identical paragraph.","Repeated identical openings create a lack of variation.","meaning")]});
D("sample",{etymology:E("From Old French essample and Latin exemplum ‘example’; English sample names a small representative amount and the acts of testing or briefly trying something.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sample"),contexts:[C("sample.s1","研究","The lab kept a water sample from each river so it could compare pollution levels later.","实验室从每条河中留取水样，以便稍后比较污染程度。","A sample is a small amount used to show or test the larger whole.","From each river distributes the collection; so states its later purpose.","Each portion represents a larger body of water.") ,C("sample.s2","研究","Before opening the full archive, the team sampled twenty files to estimate how many contained duplicate records.","打开整个档案前，团队抽查了20份文件，估计重复记录的数量。","To sample is to test a small part in order to judge the whole.","Before gives the sampling stage; to estimate gives its purpose.","The selected files stand for the larger archive.") ,C("sample.s3","飲食","At the market, shoppers sampled the new cheese before deciding whether to buy a full block.","在市场上，顾客先品尝新奶酪，再决定是否购买整块。","Sample can mean try a small amount of food or experience something briefly.","Before links tasting with the purchase decision.","The shoppers taste a small portion.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The lab tested every drop from the entire river and called the complete volume a small sample.","The lab tested a small water sample taken from the river to represent the whole.","A sample is only a small representative portion, not the entire source.")],quiz:[Q("sample.q1","sample.s1","meaning","A soil sample is ___.",["a small portion used to examine the larger area","all the soil on Earth","a formal gesture of respect"],"a small portion used to examine the larger area","The noun is a small representative amount.","meaning"),Q("sample.q2","sample.s2","context","A pollster samples a subset of voters to ___.",["estimate views in the larger population","serve them food","retire from the survey"],"estimate views in the larger population","Sampling a part helps judge the whole.","context"),Q("sample.q3","sample.s3","meaning","At a food stall, to sample a sauce is to ___.",["taste a little of it","order a full container","measure its retail price"],"taste a little of it","This is the tasting sense.","meaning"),Q("sample.q4","sample.s2","grammar","The researchers sampled ____ before drawing a conclusion.",["a small group of records","the conclusion itself","to a small group of records"],"a small group of records","Sample is transitive and takes the tested subset as its object.","grammar")]});
D("samsara",{etymology:E("From Sanskrit saṃsāra, ‘wandering through’, the cycle of death and rebirth in Hindu and Buddhist traditions from which liberation is sought.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/samsara"),contexts:[C("samsara.s1","宗教","The monk's lecture described samsara as a cycle of death and rebirth, and explained why liberation from it is sought.","僧人的讲座把轮回描述为生死再生的循环，并解释了为何人们寻求从中解脱。","Samsara is the repeating cycle of death and rebirth in which beings remain until release.","As introduces the definition; and links it to the goal of liberation.","The word refers to a religious concept, not an ordinary sequence of events.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The guide used samsara to mean one person's ordinary daily commute, with no reference to rebirth or a religious cycle.","The guide used samsara for the religious cycle of death and rebirth from which liberation is sought.","Samsara is a specific religious concept, not simply any routine journey.")],quiz:[Q("samsara.q1","samsara.s1","meaning","In Hindu and Buddhist thought, samsara refers to ___.",["the cycle of death and rebirth","a metal serving tray","a salty flavor"],"the cycle of death and rebirth","This is the central religious sense.","meaning"),Q("samsara.q2","samsara.s1","context","A text discusses release from samsara. It is discussing release from ___.",["repeated rebirth","a restaurant bill","a military salute"],"repeated rebirth","Samsara is the cycle from which release is sought.","context"),Q("samsara.q3","samsara.s1","register","Samsara is best used when discussing ___.",["South Asian religious traditions","a casual synonym for any commute","the price of a food sample"],"South Asian religious traditions","The term names a religious concept.","register"),Q("samsara.q4","samsara.s1","meaning","Which sentence uses samsara accurately?",["The teacher explained the cycle of rebirth known as samsara.","The chef called the salty soup samsara.","The guard gave a samsara to the officer."],"The teacher explained the cycle of rebirth known as samsara.","The term refers to the religious cycle of rebirth.","meaning")]});
D("sanatorium",{etymology:E("From Latin sanatorium, from sanare ‘heal’, from sanus ‘sound, healthy’; the word names an institution for rest and medical care during recovery.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sanatorium"),contexts:[C("sanatorium.s1","醫療史","In the 1930s, the mountain sanatorium offered patients fresh air, rest, and supervised treatment for tuberculosis.","20世纪30年代，山间疗养院为结核病患者提供新鲜空气、休息和监督治疗。","A sanatorium is an institution for rest and medical care during recovery.","In the 1930s sets the historical period; for identifies its patients.","The institution combined care with a restorative stay.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The patient checked into a sanatorium to buy a tray for carrying tea, rather than to rest and receive care.","The patient checked into a sanatorium to rest and receive medical care while recovering.","A sanatorium is a care institution, not a serving tray; that is a salver.")],quiz:[Q("sanatorium.q1","sanatorium.s1","meaning","A sanatorium historically provided ___.",["rest and medical care during recovery","a place to buy retail goods","a formal salute"],"rest and medical care during recovery","This matches the institution sense.","meaning"),Q("sanatorium.q2","sanatorium.s1","context","A patient recovering from a long illness stays at a sanatorium to ___.",["rest and receive supervised care","serve meals on a salver","conduct a public poll"],"rest and receive supervised care","The institution supports recovery.","context"),Q("sanatorium.q3","sanatorium.s1","word-formation","Sanatorium is related to Latin sanus, meaning ___.",["healthy or sound","salty","silent"],"healthy or sound","The word's origin is connected with healing and health.","word-formation"),Q("sanatorium.q4","sanatorium.s1","meaning","Which facility is a sanatorium?",["A recovery institution with rest and medical supervision","A shop that sells small quantities to consumers","A room with a washbasin in a station"],"A recovery institution with rest and medical supervision","A sanatorium serves people recovering from illness.","meaning")]});
D("sanctimonious",{etymology:E("From sanctimony + -ous; sanctimony derives from Late Latin sanctimonia ‘holiness’, from sanctus ‘holy’, and the adjective came to mean hypocritically self-righteous.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sanctimonious"),contexts:[C("sanctimonious.s1","性格","His sanctimonious lecture about honesty rang hollow after he had falsified the expense report himself.","他讲诚信的说教显得虚伪，因为他自己刚伪造了报销单。","Sanctimonious means hypocritically pious or self-righteous.","After gives the contradictory conduct that undermines the lecture.","His moral display conflicts with his own dishonesty.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The reviewer called the honest, modest volunteer sanctimonious even though she never claimed moral superiority or criticized anyone.","The reviewer called the volunteer sincere because she acted honestly without claiming moral superiority.","Sanctimonious implies hypocritical self-righteousness; honest modesty alone does not.")],quiz:[Q("sanctimonious.q1","sanctimonious.s1","meaning","A sanctimonious speaker often ___.",["acts morally superior while being hypocritical","quietly fixes a broken water pipe","sells goods in small amounts"],"acts morally superior while being hypocritical","The adjective is critical of hypocritical moral display.","meaning"),Q("sanctimonious.q2","sanctimonious.s1","context","Which behavior is sanctimonious?",["A person condemns others for lying while hiding their own fraud","A person admits a mistake and corrects it","A person asks for advice without judging"],"A person condemns others for lying while hiding their own fraud","The speaker's moral posture conflicts with their conduct.","context"),Q("sanctimonious.q3","sanctimonious.s1","register","Sanctimonious is generally ___.",["disapproving","a neutral medical term","a compliment for every kind act"],"disapproving","It criticizes hypocrisy and self-righteousness.","register"),Q("sanctimonious.q4","sanctimonious.s1","meaning","The sanctimonious manager ___.",["lectured staff about fairness while secretly changing their hours","apologized plainly for an error","listened without making moral claims"],"lectured staff about fairness while secretly changing their hours","The manager's conduct contradicts a show of moral superiority.","meaning")]});
D("sanction",{etymology:E("From Latin sanctio, from sancire ‘make sacred, ratify’; English developed the contrasting senses of official approval and an official penalty.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sanction"),contexts:[C("sanction.s1","國際關係","The coalition imposed trade sanctions on the regime after it ignored the cease-fire agreement.","政权无视停火协议后，联盟对其实施了贸易制裁。","A sanction can be a penalty imposed to make a country or group obey.","On the regime identifies the target; after gives the trigger.","This is the punitive noun sense.") ,C("sanction.s2","政策","The project cannot begin until it receives official sanction from the board.","项目须获得董事会正式批准后才能开始。","Sanction can mean official permission for an action.","From the board identifies the approving authority.","This is approval, opposite in tone to a penalty.") ,C("sanction.s3","治理","The council sanctioned the pilot program after reviewing its safety plan.","审查安全计划后，委员会批准了试点项目。","To sanction can mean give official approval.","The program is the direct object; after marks the review preceding approval.","This is the approving verb sense.") ,C("sanction.s4","治理","The regulator sanctioned the company with a fine for repeatedly hiding safety defects.","监管机构因该公司反复隐瞒安全缺陷而对其处以罚款。","To sanction can also mean punish using official penalties.","With a fine gives the penalty; for states the offense.","This is the punitive verb sense.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The board sanctioned the project as a penalty by granting it the official permission it had requested.","The board sanctioned the project by granting its official approval.","Sanction is ambiguous: grant approval is not the same as imposing a penalty; the sentence must clarify the intended sense.")],quiz:[Q("sanction.q1","sanction.s1","meaning","Economic sanctions imposed on a country are ___.",["official penalties intended to pressure it","a tray used to serve letters","formal permission to begin a project"],"official penalties intended to pressure it","This is the punitive noun sense.","meaning"),Q("sanction.q2","sanction.s2","context","The plan awaits the board's sanction. It awaits ___.",["official permission","a fine for breaking a rule","a survey sample"],"official permission","This is the approval noun sense.","context"),Q("sanction.q3","sanction.s3","grammar","Choose the sentence where sanction means approve.",["The board sanctioned the safety trial.","The regulator sanctioned the firm with a fine.","The coalition imposed sanctions on the state."],"The board sanctioned the safety trial.","Here sanctioned means gave official approval.","grammar"),Q("sanction.q4","sanction.s4","meaning","A regulator sanctioned a firm with a fine. The regulator ___.",["punished it officially","gave it permission to start","praised its volunteers"],"punished it officially","This is the punitive verb sense.","meaning")]});
D("sanctity",{etymology:E("From Latin sanctitas, from sanctus ‘holy’; the noun means holiness or a state considered too important and inviolable to violate.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sanctity"),contexts:[C("sanctity.s1","法律","The court emphasized the sanctity of private medical records when it rejected the unauthorized disclosure.","法院驳回未经授权的披露时，强调了私人医疗记录不可侵犯的重要性。","Sanctity is holiness or the quality of being inviolable and deeply important.","When introduces the court's action; of private medical records names what is protected.","The records must be treated as inviolable.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The committee described the sanctity of the archive as permission to alter every original document without review.","The committee protected the sanctity of the archive by requiring careful review before any original document was altered.","Sanctity means holiness or inviolable importance, not unrestricted permission to damage what is protected.")],quiz:[Q("sanctity.q1","sanctity.s1","meaning","The sanctity of a promise refers to its ___.",["sacred or inviolable importance","salt content","retail value"],"sacred or inviolable importance","Sanctity describes something treated as deeply important and not to be violated.","meaning"),Q("sanctity.q2","sanctity.s1","context","A community protects the sanctity of a memorial by ___.",["treating it as a place of deep respect","using it as a noisy marketplace","changing its meaning for a joke"],"treating it as a place of deep respect","The memorial is regarded as inviolable and important.","context"),Q("sanctity.q3","sanctity.s1","word-formation","Sanctity is related to the adjective ___.",["sanct","same","salty"],"sanct","The Latin source is sanctus, ‘holy’; English sanctity names holiness.","word-formation"),Q("sanctity.q4","sanctity.s1","meaning","Which phrase best captures sanctity?",["the inviolable value of a person's private records","the exact amount of salt in a soup","the number of visitors in a shop"],"the inviolable value of a person's private records","Sanctity concerns holiness or inviolable importance.","meaning")]});
D("sanctuary",{etymology:E("From Latin sanctuarium, from sanctus ‘holy’; the word first named a sacred place and also developed senses of refuge and a protected wildlife area.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sanctuary"),contexts:[C("sanctuary.s1","宗教","Pilgrims left their shoes at the entrance before entering the sanctuary of the temple.","朝圣者在进入寺庙的圣所前把鞋留在入口处。","A sanctuary can be the most holy part of a religious building.","Of the temple identifies the building; before gives the order of entry.","This is the sacred-place sense.") ,C("sanctuary.s2","救援","The family found sanctuary in a school gym after the wildfire made their home unsafe.","野火使家园变得危险后，这家人在学校体育馆找到了避难所。","Sanctuary can be a place of safety for people in danger.","After explains why the family needed shelter.","This is the refuge sense.") ,C("sanctuary.s3","保育","The wetland sanctuary gives migrating cranes a protected place to feed and nest.","湿地保护区为迁徙的鹤提供了觅食和筑巢的安全场所。","A sanctuary can be an area where wild animals are protected.","For migrating cranes names the wildlife served.","This is the conservation-area sense.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The injured family sought sanctuary in the burning house rather than a place of safety.","The injured family sought sanctuary in the school shelter away from the burning house.","A sanctuary is a safe place; a burning home is dangerous rather than protective.")],quiz:[Q("sanctuary.q1","sanctuary.s1","meaning","The sanctuary of a church is ___.",["its most holy area","a place where goods are sold retail","a salty cooking ingredient"],"its most holy area","This is the religious-building sense.","meaning"),Q("sanctuary.q2","sanctuary.s2","context","A family escaping a flood finds sanctuary at a safe school. The school is ___.",["a refuge from danger","a wildlife hunting ground","a formal salute"],"a refuge from danger","This is the safety sense.","context"),Q("sanctuary.q3","sanctuary.s3","meaning","A bird sanctuary is an area where birds are ___.",["protected","sold as food","required to migrate immediately"],"protected","This is the wildlife-preservation sense.","meaning"),Q("sanctuary.q4","sanctuary.s2","collocation","The displaced residents sought ____ from the storm.",["sanctuary","sameness","salver"],"sanctuary","Seek sanctuary means look for a place of safety.","collocation")]});
D("sand",{etymology:E("From Old English sand, of Germanic origin and related to words in other Germanic languages; it names loose grains and the areas they cover.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sand"),contexts:[C("sand.s1","地質","The filter trapped coarse sand before the water reached the storage tank.","水进入储水罐前，过滤器截住了粗沙。","Sand is tiny loose grains of rock or mineral.","Before marks the order in the treatment system.","The material consists of small grains.") ,C("sand.s2","海岸","At low tide, children built a channel across the wide sand beside the bay.","退潮时，孩子们在海湾旁宽阔的沙滩上挖了一条水道。","Sand can mean an area covered by those grains, especially a beach.","Across the wide sand describes the stretch of shore they used.","This is the landform sense.")],mistakes:[M("countability","The builder ordered two sand for the foundation.","The builder ordered two loads of sand for the foundation.","Sand as a material is normally uncountable; countable deliveries need a unit such as loads.")],quiz:[Q("sand.q1","sand.s1","meaning","Geologists study sand when they examine ___.",["small loose mineral grains","a country's economic sanctions","a ceremonial salute"],"small loose mineral grains","This is the material sense.","meaning"),Q("sand.q2","sand.s2","context","A picnic on the sand beside the sea takes place on ___.",["a beach or sandy shore","a serving tray","a medical recovery ward"],"a beach or sandy shore","Sand can name a shore area covered with grains.","context"),Q("sand.q3","sand.s1","countability","The builders ordered three ____ of sand.",["loads","sandses","sand"],"loads","Use a measure such as loads to count uncountable sand.","countability"),Q("sand.q4","sand.s2","meaning","Which use refers to a place rather than loose grains as material?",["They walked along the golden sand.","Sand clogged the water filter.","The sand was mixed into concrete."],"They walked along the golden sand.","Here sand means a sandy area or beach.","meaning")]});
