D("sandal",{etymology:E("From Greek sandalion, a diminutive of σανδάλιον, through Latin sandalium; it names an open shoe with a sole held by straps.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sandal"),contexts:[C("sandal.s1","服裝","Mira wore a leather sandal with two straps while walking along the warm beach.","天气温暖时，Mira 穿着一只双带皮凉鞋沿海滩散步。","A sandal is an open shoe whose sole is held to the foot by straps.","With two straps describes how it is fastened.","The heel and much of the foot remain open.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","He laced up his closed leather boot and called it a sandal because it covered his ankle completely.","He fastened the open shoe with straps and called it a sandal.","A sandal is open and held by straps; a fully enclosed ankle boot is a different kind of shoe.")],quiz:[Q("sandal.q1","sandal.s1","meaning","A sandal is usually ___.",["an open shoe held on by straps","a closed boot with a high shaft","a flat tray for carrying cups"],"an open shoe held on by straps","The defining construction is a sole with straps.","meaning"),Q("sandal.q2","sandal.s1","context","Which footwear is a sandal?",["A sole attached with two crossing straps","A fully enclosed hiking boot","A sock with no sole"],"A sole attached with two crossing straps","The open strapped design matches a sandal.","context"),Q("sandal.q3","sandal.s1","plural","She packed two ____ for the trip.",["sandals","sandal's","sandal"],"sandals","Two requires the plural form sandals.","plural"),Q("sandal.q4","sandal.s1","meaning","A sandal differs from a boot because it ___.",["leaves much of the foot open","always has a metal toe","is filled with saltwater"],"leaves much of the foot open","Sandals are open footwear secured by straps.","meaning")]});
D("sandbank",{etymology:E("A compound of sand + bank; bank comes from a Germanic word for a raised edge or ridge, and a sandbank is a water-built accumulation that may be hidden.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sandbank"),contexts:[C("sandbank.s1","航運","The pilot slowed the ferry when a low tide exposed a sandbank near the channel entrance.","入口附近的沙洲在退潮时露出水面，船长便让渡轮减速。","A sandbank is a bank of sand built up by water and potentially hazardous to boats.","When gives the condition that reveals the hazard.","The shallow ridge lies under or near navigable water.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The ferry crossed safely over the deep open channel, and the pilot called the deep water a sandbank even though no sand ridge was present.","The pilot warned that a shallow sandbank had formed near the channel entrance.","A sandbank is a raised accumulation of sand, often dangerous when concealed in water.")],quiz:[Q("sandbank.q1","sandbank.s1","meaning","A submerged sandbank can be dangerous because it ___.",["creates a shallow obstacle for boats","is a deep ocean trench","is a type of shoe"],"creates a shallow obstacle for boats","A water-built ridge may lie hidden near the surface.","meaning"),Q("sandbank.q2","sandbank.s1","context","A pilot checks a chart for sandbanks before entering a harbor to avoid ___.",["running aground on shallow sand","losing a shoe strap","sampling the water's taste"],"running aground on shallow sand","Sandbanks are shallow ridges that threaten boats.","context"),Q("sandbank.q3","sandbank.s1","word-formation","Sandbank combines sand with a word for ___.",["a raised ridge or edge","a medical institution","a formal gesture"],"a raised ridge or edge","Bank here names the raised formation.","word-formation"),Q("sandbank.q4","sandbank.s1","meaning","Which feature is a sandbank?",["A ridge of sand built up in a river","A deep hole in solid rock","A pile of dry leaves"],"A ridge of sand built up in a river","Water can deposit sand into a raised bank.","meaning")]});
D("sandbar",{etymology:E("A compound of sand + bar, where bar means a ridge or shoal across water; it names a narrow deposit along a channel or shore.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sandbar"),contexts:[C("sandbar.s1","河流","At low water, the canoe scraped across a sandbar that stretched from the river bend toward the opposite bank.","水位低时，独木舟擦过一条从河弯伸向对岸的沙洲。","A sandbar is a bar of sand across or along a channel or shore.","That-clause describes the bar's position; at low water gives the condition.","The shallow ridge crosses part of the river.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The fishing boat passed over a deep, bottomless trench, which the map labeled a sandbar.","The fishing boat passed over a shallow ridge of deposited sand, which the map labeled a sandbar.","A sandbar is a shallow sandy bar, not a deep trench.")],quiz:[Q("sandbar.q1","sandbar.s1","meaning","A sandbar is ___.",["a ridge of sand in or beside a waterway","a deep part of the sea","a tray used by a server"],"a ridge of sand in or beside a waterway","The compound names a sandy bar or shoal.","meaning"),Q("sandbar.q2","sandbar.s1","context","A swimmer walks on a sandbar at low tide when it is ___.",["a shallow raised stretch of sand","a high mountain ridge","a room in a sanatorium"],"a shallow raised stretch of sand","The sandbar can become exposed as water falls.","context"),Q("sandbar.q3","sandbar.s1","word-formation","In sandbar, bar means ___.",["a ridge or shoal","a serving dish","a medical rest"],"a ridge or shoal","The word bar names the raised or shallow formation.","word-formation"),Q("sandbar.q4","sandbar.s1","meaning","Which boat hazard is a sandbar?",["A shallow sandy ridge crossing a channel","A deep trench far offshore","A floating wooden dock"],"A shallow sandy ridge crossing a channel","A sandbar can obstruct a channel.","meaning")]});
D("sandstone",{etymology:E("A compound of sand + stone; geologists use it for rock formed when sand grains are compacted and cemented together.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sandstone"),contexts:[C("sandstone.s1","地質","The cliff's sandstone layers preserved ripple marks left by an ancient shallow sea.","峭壁中的砂岩层保存了古代浅海留下的波纹印迹。","Sandstone is rock formed from compacted sand, often in visible layers.","Left by identifies the origin of the marks; ancient describes their age.","The sedimentary rock preserves earlier surface patterns.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The geologist identified the loose beach grains as sandstone before any of them had been compacted into rock.","The geologist identified the compacted, cemented beach grains as sandstone after they had formed rock.","Sandstone is consolidated rock, not loose sand grains.")],quiz:[Q("sandstone.q1","sandstone.s1","meaning","Sandstone forms when sand grains ___.",["become compacted and cemented into rock","remain loose and dry on a beach","turn into saltwater"],"become compacted and cemented into rock","The rock consists of consolidated sand grains.","meaning"),Q("sandstone.q2","sandstone.s1","context","A building made of sandstone uses ___.",["sedimentary rock formed from sand","a fabric woven from seaweed","a metal serving tray"],"sedimentary rock formed from sand","This matches the geological sense.","context"),Q("sandstone.q3","sandstone.s1","word-formation","Sandstone is a compound of sand and ___.",["stone","storm","shore"],"stone","The second element names the rock material.","word-formation"),Q("sandstone.q4","sandstone.s1","meaning","Which sample is sandstone?",["A cemented rock with visible sand grains","Loose sand in a bucket","A block of pure ice"],"A cemented rock with visible sand grains","Sandstone is consolidated sedimentary rock.","meaning")]});
D("sandwich",{etymology:E("Named after John Montagu, 4th Earl of Sandwich (1718–1792), whose title became associated with bread enclosing a filling; the verb later extended to place something between two others.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sandwich"),contexts:[C("sandwich.s1","飲食","For lunch, Ravi packed a sandwich of roasted vegetables and cheese between slices of rye bread.","午餐时，Ravi 把烤蔬菜和奶酪夹在两片黑麦面包之间，做成三明治。","A sandwich is two pieces of bread with food between them.","Of introduces the filling; between locates it inside the bread.","The food is enclosed by two bread pieces.") ,C("sandwich.s2","空間","The tiny café was sandwiched between a pharmacy and a bookshop on the narrow street.","这家小咖啡馆被夹在狭窄街道上的药店和书店之间。","To sandwich something is to put it tightly between two others.","Between names the two surrounding buildings.","This is the figurative placement verb.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","The café was sandwich between a pharmacy and a bookshop on the narrow street.","The café was sandwiched between a pharmacy and a bookshop on the narrow street.","The passive verb requires the past participle sandwiched.")],quiz:[Q("sandwich.q1","sandwich.s1","meaning","A sandwich has ___.",["food between pieces of bread","sand inside a glass jar","a serving tray under every ingredient"],"food between pieces of bread","This is the common food sense.","meaning"),Q("sandwich.q2","sandwich.s2","context","A house sandwiched between two shops is ___.",["tightly located between them","made from bread and cheese","far from both shops"],"tightly located between them","The verb means place between two things.","context"),Q("sandwich.q3","sandwich.s1","countability","She made three ____ for the picnic.",["sandwiches","sandwich","sandwich's"],"sandwiches","The plural of sandwich is sandwiches.","countability"),Q("sandwich.q4","sandwich.s2","grammar","The cottage is ____ between two tall trees.",["sandwiched","sandwich","sandwiching"],"sandwiched","The passive construction uses sandwiched.","grammar")]});
D("sandy",{etymology:E("From sand + adjective-forming -y; the Old English noun sand is of Germanic origin.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sandy"),contexts:[C("sandy.s1","地理","The sandy path ended at a dune where the wind had piled fine grains against the fence.","沙质小路通向一座沙丘，风把细沙堆在篱笆边。","Sandy means consisting of, covered with, or like sand.","Where introduces the path's endpoint; where the wind clause describes the dune.","The adjective describes the path's loose-grained surface.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The rocky trail was sandy, covered only in large solid boulders with no loose grains.","The rocky trail was stony, covered only in large solid boulders with no loose grains.","Sandy describes sand or a sand-like surface; large boulders make a trail stony.")],quiz:[Q("sandy.q1","sandy.s1","meaning","A sandy beach is ___.",["covered with sand","made of pure ice","full of metal tools"],"covered with sand","Sandy describes a surface containing or covered by sand.","meaning"),Q("sandy.q2","sandy.s1","context","Which ground is sandy?",["Fine loose grains stick to the hikers' shoes.","Bare rock forms the entire path.","A tiled floor is polished smooth."],"Fine loose grains stick to the hikers' shoes.","Loose sand covers the route.","context"),Q("sandy.q3","sandy.s1","word-formation","The suffix -y in sandy forms an adjective meaning ___.",["having or covered with sand","without sand","the act of measuring sand"],"having or covered with sand","The suffix -y often means having or characterized by something.","word-formation"),Q("sandy.q4","sandy.s1","meaning","A sandy soil contains many ___.",["sand grains","salute gestures","sapphire gems"],"sand grains","Sandy means consisting partly of sand.","meaning")]});
D("sane",{etymology:E("From Latin sanus ‘healthy, sound’, through French sain; the adjective describes a sound mind and, figuratively, sensible judgment.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sane"),contexts:[C("sane.s1","健康","After weeks without sleep, the doctor urged him to seek help before the exhaustion affected his ability to think clearly and stay sane.","连续数周睡眠不足后，医生劝他在疲惫影响清晰思考和心理健康前寻求帮助。","Sane can mean not mentally ill and of sound mind.","Before introduces prevention; and joins clear thinking with mental health.","The sentence uses the literal mental-health sense respectfully.") ,C("sane.s2","決策","Choosing a backup route before the mountain pass closes is a sane precaution.","在山口关闭前选好备用路线，是明智的预防措施。","Sane can mean sensible and reasonable rather than extreme.","Before gives the reason for taking the precaution.","This is the figurative judgment sense.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The planner called a wildly risky, unsupported scheme sane because it ignored every safety concern.","The planner called the cautious, evidence-based scheme sane because it addressed the safety concerns.","Sane in the reasonable sense describes sound judgment, not reckless disregard.")],quiz:[Q("sane.q1","sane.s1","meaning","Of sound mind means ___.",["mentally healthy and able to think clearly","covered with sand","ready to retire from a sport"],"mentally healthy and able to think clearly","This is the literal sense of sane.","meaning"),Q("sane.q2","sane.s2","context","A sane budget plan is one that is ___.",["reasonable and not extreme","impossible to pay for","made from sapphire"],"reasonable and not extreme","This is the figurative sensible-judgment sense.","context"),Q("sane.q3","sane.s2","collocation","Given the short deadline, a ____ choice is to simplify the design.",["sane","sandy","sardine"],"sane","A sane choice is sensible under the circumstances.","collocation"),Q("sane.q4","sane.s1","register","When discussing mental health, sane should be used ___.",["carefully and without labeling people dismissively","as a joke about anyone who disagrees","as a substitute for a diagnosis"],"carefully and without labeling people dismissively","The literal sense concerns mental health; avoid using it to stigmatize people.","register")]});
D("sanguinariness",{etymology:E("From sanguinary + -ness; sanguinary comes from Latin sanguinarius ‘bloody’, from sanguis ‘blood’, and the noun names bloodthirsty character or slaughter.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sanguinary"),contexts:[C("sanguinariness.s1","文學","The historian noted the sanguinariness of the battle chronicle, which dwelt on casualties rather than strategy.","历史学家指出，这部战役编年史嗜血残酷，篇幅集中描写伤亡而非战略。","Sanguinariness is bloodthirsty character or the quality of involving slaughter.","Which clause explains the historian's evaluation.","The term criticizes the text's fixation on bloodshed.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The reviewer praised the novel's sanguinariness because it avoided violence and focused entirely on peaceful gardening.","The reviewer criticized the novel's sanguinariness because it dwelt on violent slaughter.","Sanguinariness means bloodthirsty or involving slaughter, the opposite of peaceful gardening.")],quiz:[Q("sanguinariness.q1","sanguinariness.s1","meaning","A story's sanguinariness refers to its ___.",["bloodthirsty or slaughter-filled quality","calm kindness toward every character","salt content"],"bloodthirsty or slaughter-filled quality","The noun names bloody, violent character.","meaning"),Q("sanguinariness.q2","sanguinariness.s1","context","A critic calls a chronicle sanguinariness excessive when it ___.",["dwells on massacres and casualties","omits every description of violence","describes a beach covered in sand"],"dwells on massacres and casualties","The text emphasizes slaughter.","context"),Q("sanguinariness.q3","sanguinariness.s1","word-formation","Sanguinariness is formed from sanguinary plus ___.",["-ness","-less","-ly"],"-ness","The suffix forms a noun naming the quality.","word-formation"),Q("sanguinariness.q4","sanguinariness.s1","meaning","Which account is most likely described as sanguinary?",["A battle record focused on extensive bloodshed","A peaceful diary about gardening","A safety guide for first aid"],"A battle record focused on extensive bloodshed","The word is associated with bloodshed and slaughter.","meaning")]});
D("sanitary",{etymology:E("From French sanitaire and Latin sanitarius, from sanitas ‘health’, related to sanus ‘healthy’; the adjective concerns cleanliness, health, or sanitation systems.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sanitary"),contexts:[C("sanitary.s1","食品","Inspectors rejected the kitchen because its water containers were not sanitary enough to protect customers from disease.","检查员拒绝通过这间厨房，因为储水容器不够卫生，无法保护顾客免受疾病侵害。","Sanitary means clean enough to protect health and prevent disease.","Because explains why the kitchen failed inspection.","This is the cleanliness standard sense.") ,C("sanitary.s2","工程","The town approved a sanitary sewer project to carry wastewater away from homes.","镇里批准了卫生排污工程，以便把污水从住宅区排走。","Sanitary can relate to systems that keep places clean and healthy.","To carry states the sewer system's purpose.","This is the public-health infrastructure sense.") ,C("sanitary.s3","用法","In some American English, a station sign marked sanitary points visitors to a public toilet.","在部分美式英语中，车站标有 sanitary 的指示牌会把游客引向公共厕所。","As a noun in American English, a sanitary can mean a public toilet.","In some American English limits the usage; marked describes the sign.","This is a regional noun use, uncommon elsewhere.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The kitchen was sanitary because dirty water sat uncovered beside the food-preparation counter.","The kitchen was unsanitary because dirty water sat uncovered beside the food-preparation counter.","Sanitary means sufficiently clean to protect health; uncovered dirty water creates an unsanitary condition.")],quiz:[Q("sanitary.q1","sanitary.s1","meaning","A sanitary kitchen is ___.",["clean enough to protect health","filled with untreated sewage","covered in sand"],"clean enough to protect health","This is the health-protecting cleanliness sense.","meaning"),Q("sanitary.q2","sanitary.s2","context","A sanitary sewer carries ___.",["wastewater away from homes","fresh fruit to a market","survey responses to an office"],"wastewater away from homes","Sanitary systems protect public health through waste services.","context"),Q("sanitary.q3","sanitary.s3","register","In some American English, a sanitary may refer to ___.",["a public toilet","a clean kitchen","a wastewater pipe only"],"a public toilet","This regional noun use means public toilet.","register"),Q("sanitary.q4","sanitary.s1","meaning","Which inspection result is sanitary?",["Clean containers prevent contamination of drinking water.","Open sewage flows beside food.","The kitchen has no way to wash hands."],"Clean containers prevent contamination of drinking water.","The clean condition helps prevent disease.","meaning")]});
D("sanitation",{etymology:E("From sanitary + -ation, a noun-forming suffix; sanitary comes from Latin sanitarius, from sanitas ‘health’.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sanitation"),contexts:[C("sanitation.s1","公共衛生","The island's sanitation service removed waste and tested drinking water after the storm damaged pipes.","风暴损坏管道后，岛上的卫生服务清运了垃圾并检测饮用水。","Sanitation includes equipment and services that protect public health, especially waste and water systems.","After states the emergency prompting the service.","This sense refers to public-health infrastructure.") ,C("sanitation.s2","食品","Frequent handwashing is a basic sanitation practice in the bakery's kitchen.","经常洗手是面包店厨房的基本卫生做法。","Sanitation can mean the practice of keeping places clean and free of germs.","In the kitchen identifies where the practice applies.","This is the cleaning practice sense.")],mistakes:[M("word form","Good sanitation in the kitchen reduce the risk of food-borne illness.","Good sanitation in the kitchen reduces the risk of food-borne illness.","Sanitation is a singular uncountable noun and takes reduces.")],quiz:[Q("sanitation.q1","sanitation.s1","meaning","A city's sanitation department usually manages ___.",["waste removal and public-health services","military salutes","sandstone quarries only"],"waste removal and public-health services","This is the infrastructure/service sense.","meaning"),Q("sanitation.q2","sanitation.s2","context","A food worker follows sanitation practices by ___.",["washing hands and cleaning equipment","leaving spoiled food uncovered","wearing a sapphire ring"],"washing hands and cleaning equipment","Sanitation also means practices that reduce germs.","context"),Q("sanitation.q3","sanitation.s1","collocation","Reliable water and waste ____ protect community health.",["sanitation","sarcasm","salver"],"sanitation","Water and waste sanitation is a public-health phrase.","collocation"),Q("sanitation.q4","sanitation.s2","meaning","Which is a sanitation practice?",["Disinfecting the cutting board between foods","Storing dirty water beside clean cups","Ignoring handwashing after handling waste"],"Disinfecting the cutting board between foods","Cleaning practice helps keep germs from spreading.","meaning")]});
D("sanity",{etymology:E("From Latin sanitas ‘health, soundness’, related to sanus ‘healthy’; the noun names mental health or sensible judgment.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sanity"),contexts:[C("sanity.s1","健康","After the exhausting crisis passed, Maya spoke with her doctor about restoring her sleep and sanity.","危机造成的极度疲惫过去后，Maya 与医生讨论如何恢复睡眠和心理健康。","Sanity can mean a healthy and normal mind.","Restoring links sleep and mental well-being as things she needs back.","This is the mental-health sense.") ,C("sanity.s2","工作","The project manager added a simple checklist as a sanity check before approving the unusual figures.","项目经理在批准这些异常数据前加了一份简单清单，作为合理性检查。","Sanity can mean sensible and reasonable judgment in everyday decisions.","As a sanity check identifies the checklist's function.","This is the figurative reasonableness sense.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The team performed a sanity check by approving figures that contradicted every source and had no explanation.","The team performed a sanity check by comparing the figures with reliable sources before approval.","A sanity check tests whether something is reasonable; ignoring contradictions does not do that.")],quiz:[Q("sanity.q1","sanity.s1","meaning","In a health context, sanity refers to ___.",["a healthy and normal mind","the amount of salt in food","a legal penalty"],"a healthy and normal mind","This is the mental-health sense.","meaning"),Q("sanity.q2","sanity.s2","context","A sanity check on a budget asks whether the figures are ___.",["reasonable and plausible","made of stone","a public toilet"],"reasonable and plausible","This is the everyday judgment sense.","context"),Q("sanity.q3","sanity.s2","collocation","Before submitting the totals, we did a quick ____ check.",["sanity","sandbank","salvation"],"sanity","A sanity check is a review for reasonableness.","collocation"),Q("sanity.q4","sanity.s1","register","When discussing a person's mental health, sanity should be used ___.",["carefully and respectfully","as a joke about disagreement","as a substitute for clinical assessment"],"carefully and respectfully","The term can refer to mental health and should not stigmatize people.","register")]});
D("sap",{etymology:E("From Old English sæp, of Germanic origin; English uses it for plant fluid, a person's energy, and the act of gradually draining strength.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sap"),contexts:[C("sap.s1","植物學","In spring, rising sap carries water and nutrients from the roots toward the new leaves.","春天，流动的树液把水分和养料从根部输送到新叶。","Sap is liquid that moves through a plant and carries food to growing parts.","From the roots and toward the leaves describe its route.","This is the plant-fluid sense.") ,C("sap.s2","體力","The long evacuation had taken the sap out of the volunteers, who paused to drink and rest.","漫长的疏散工作耗尽了志愿者的精力，他们停下来喝水休息。","Sap can mean the strength and energy a person needs to act.","Taken the sap out is an idiom; who-clause shows the fatigue.","This is the vitality sense.") ,C("sap.s3","組織","Repeated emergency meetings sapped the small team's energy before the inspection began.","检查开始前，反复的紧急会议耗尽了小组的精力。","To sap means drain strength or energy away.","Sapped takes energy as its object; before gives the timing.","The meetings gradually reduce the team's capacity.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The overnight workload sapped the team's energy by restoring everyone's strength and leaving them fully refreshed.","The overnight workload sapped the team's energy and left them exhausted.","Sap means drain strength, not restore it.")],quiz:[Q("sap.q1","sap.s1","meaning","Plant sap is ___.",["fluid that carries nutrients through a plant","a stone used in a wall","a salty sauce"],"fluid that carries nutrients through a plant","This is the botanical sense.","meaning"),Q("sap.q2","sap.s2","context","After a demanding hike, the group felt the sap had gone out of them. They felt ___.",["tired and low on energy","full of new strength","ready to salute the guide"],"tired and low on energy","Sap can mean a person's vitality.","context"),Q("sap.q3","sap.s3","grammar","The heat ____ energy from the workers.",["sapped","sap","sapping to"],"sapped","Sap is a transitive verb taking energy as its object.","grammar"),Q("sap.q4","sap.s3","meaning","Which event can sap a team's strength?",["A week of sleepless emergency shifts","A full day of restful sleep","A short break with water"],"A week of sleepless emergency shifts","The verb means drain energy.","meaning")]});
D("sapience",{etymology:E("From Latin sapientia ‘wisdom’, from sapiens, present participle of sapere ‘be wise, taste’; English uses it for deep or elevated wisdom.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sapience"),contexts:[C("sapience.s1","哲學","The elder's sapience showed in her ability to connect the village's history with the choices facing its young leaders.","长者能把村庄历史与年轻领导者面临的选择联系起来，显示出深刻的智慧。","Sapience is wisdom, especially of a deep or elevated kind.","In her ability explains how that wisdom appeared.","The term is more formal than everyday common sense.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The committee called the shallow guess sapience even though it was unsupported and showed no insight.","The committee called the well-considered insight sapience because it reflected deep wisdom.","Sapience means deep wisdom; a baseless guess does not show it.")],quiz:[Q("sapience.q1","sapience.s1","meaning","Sapience is closest in meaning to ___.",["deep wisdom","a young tree","a sarcastic remark"],"deep wisdom","The noun names elevated wisdom.","meaning"),Q("sapience.q2","sapience.s1","context","A philosopher's sapience is evident when the philosopher ___.",["offers a far-sighted, thoughtful judgment","repeats a rumor without checking it","serves soup on a tray"],"offers a far-sighted, thoughtful judgment","This is deep and considered wisdom.","context"),Q("sapience.q3","sapience.s1","register","Sapience is a relatively ____ word for wisdom.",["formal or literary","casual slang for salt","medical name for a restroom"],"formal or literary","Sapience is more elevated in register than ordinary wisdom.","register"),Q("sapience.q4","sapience.s1","meaning","Which quality best demonstrates sapience?",["Understanding a difficult issue with depth and judgment","Memorizing one number without context","Speaking in a mocking tone"],"Understanding a difficult issue with depth and judgment","The word refers to deep wisdom.","meaning")]});
D("sapiens",{etymology:E("From Latin sapiens ‘wise’, the present participle of sapere ‘be wise’; it appears in the scientific species name Homo sapiens.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sapiens"),contexts:[C("sapiens.s1","生物學","The museum label identifies the fossil as Homo sapiens and explains that the species name means ‘wise human’.","博物馆标签把这块化石标为 Homo sapiens，并解释该物种名称意为“有智慧的人”。","Sapiens in the species name means belonging to the human species Homo sapiens.","As introduces the label's classification; that-clause explains the name.","It is a taxonomic adjective, not an everyday synonym for a wise person.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The zoologist labeled the fossil Homo sapiens, a species of saltwater fish.","The zoologist labeled the fossil Homo sapiens, the scientific species name for modern humans.","Homo sapiens names the human species, not a fish.")],quiz:[Q("sapiens.q1","sapiens.s1","meaning","In Homo sapiens, sapiens is the species epithet for ___.",["modern humans","a saltwater fish","a kind of sandstone"],"modern humans","The term is used in the scientific name of humans.","meaning"),Q("sapiens.q2","sapiens.s1","context","A museum uses Homo sapiens on a human fossil label because the name identifies ___.",["the human species","a public-health system","a blue gemstone"],"the human species","This is the taxonomic use.","context"),Q("sapiens.q3","sapiens.s1","register","Sapiens is most commonly encountered in ___.",["the scientific name Homo sapiens","a casual greeting","a recipe for a sandwich"],"the scientific name Homo sapiens","It is a Latin species epithet in taxonomy.","register"),Q("sapiens.q4","sapiens.s1","meaning","What does the Latin adjective sapiens traditionally mean?",["wise","sandy","salty"],"wise","Sapiens is the participle of sapere, ‘be wise’.","meaning")]});
D("sapling",{etymology:E("From sap + diminutive suffix -ling; Old English sapling referred to a young tree, with the ending indicating a small or young form.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sapling"),contexts:[C("sapling.s1","林業","The volunteers protected each sapling with a mesh guard so deer would not strip its tender bark.","志愿者给每棵树苗套上网罩，防止鹿啃掉其柔嫩树皮。","A sapling is a young, immature tree with a thin trunk.","So gives the purpose of the mesh guard.","The tree is still young and needs protection.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The forester called the ancient oak with its massive trunk a sapling, although it had stood for centuries.","The forester called the young tree with its thin trunk a sapling.","A sapling is a young, not-yet-mature tree; an ancient oak is mature.")],quiz:[Q("sapling.q1","sapling.s1","meaning","A sapling is ___.",["a young tree with a thin trunk","a fully grown forest","fluid inside a mature tree"],"a young tree with a thin trunk","The noun means a young, immature tree.","meaning"),Q("sapling.q2","sapling.s1","context","A gardener stakes a sapling because ___.",["the young tree needs support as it grows","the tree is a serving tray","its bark is made of sapphire"],"the young tree needs support as it grows","Young trees can be fragile and need support.","context"),Q("sapling.q3","sapling.s1","word-formation","The ending -ling in sapling helps signal ___.",["a young or small form","a formal penalty","a quality of wisdom"],"a young or small form","The suffix forms a diminutive or young form.","word-formation"),Q("sapling.q4","sapling.s1","meaning","Which is most likely a sapling?",["A newly planted birch with a slender trunk","A centuries-old oak","A fallen stone column"],"A newly planted birch with a slender trunk","Saplings are young trees not yet mature.","meaning")]});
D("sapphire",{etymology:E("From Greek sappheiros through Latin sapphirus; the ancient gem name may first have referred to a different blue stone before being applied to corundum.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sapphire"),contexts:[C("sapphire.s1","珠寶","The jeweler set a deep-blue sapphire in a silver ring and checked the stone for cracks under a lamp.","珠宝商把一颗深蓝色蓝宝石镶进银戒指，并在灯下检查宝石是否有裂痕。","A sapphire is a precious gem of corundum, typically deep blue.","In a silver ring gives its setting; under a lamp gives the inspection method.","This is the gemstone noun sense.") ,C("sapphire.s2","色彩","At dusk, the lake turned sapphire beneath the clear western sky.","黄昏时，湖面在晴朗的西方天空下变成了明亮的深蓝色。","Sapphire can be an adjective describing a bright deep blue.","Beneath locates the color; turned marks its change.","This is the color adjective sense.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The jeweler called the bright red ruby sapphire, although sapphire describes a deep-blue corundum gem.","The jeweler called the bright red ruby a ruby; sapphire usually names a blue corundum gem.","Sapphire is typically deep blue; a bright red corundum gem is a ruby.")],quiz:[Q("sapphire.q1","sapphire.s1","meaning","A sapphire is a precious variety of ___.",["corundum","sandstone","salver"],"corundum","The gemstone sense is a form of corundum.","meaning"),Q("sapphire.q2","sapphire.s2","context","A sapphire sea is ___.",["bright deep blue","pale green","covered in dry sand"],"bright deep blue","Sapphire can describe a vivid deep-blue color.","context"),Q("sapphire.q3","sapphire.s1","meaning","Which object contains a sapphire?",["A ring set with a deep-blue precious stone","A shoe held by straps","A public sanitation pipe"],"A ring set with a deep-blue precious stone","This is the gemstone noun sense.","meaning"),Q("sapphire.q4","sapphire.s2","word-choice","The painter used a ____ shade for the deep-blue night sky.",["sapphire","sardine","sanitary"],"sapphire","Sapphire is used adjectivally for bright deep blue.","word-choice")]});
D("sarcasm",{etymology:E("From Greek sarkasmos, from sarkazein ‘tear flesh, speak bitterly’; the word came to mean mocking language whose intended meaning is often opposite to its words.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sarcasm"),contexts:[C("sarcasm.s1","對話","After the printer jammed for the third time, Jo said, “Wonderful timing,” using sarcasm to show annoyance.","打印机第三次卡住后，Jo 说“时间真好”，用反话表达恼火。","Sarcasm is language whose intended meaning mocks or contradicts the literal words.","After sets the frustrating event; to show explains the ironic purpose.","The praise is opposite to the speaker's real evaluation.") ,C("sarcasm.s2","性格","Her constant sarcasm made new colleagues unsure whether she was joking or criticizing them.","她总是讽刺，使新同事拿不准她是在开玩笑还是在批评他们。","Sarcasm can be the habit of making mocking remarks.","Made ... unsure describes the effect of the habit.","This is the disposition to use such remarks.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","He used sarcasm when he sincerely said the repair was excellent and intended no mockery or opposite meaning.","He used praise rather than sarcasm when he sincerely said the repair was excellent.","Sarcasm involves mockery or an intended meaning different from the literal words.")],quiz:[Q("sarcasm.q1","sarcasm.s1","meaning","After a long delay, saying “How wonderfully punctual” may be sarcasm if the speaker means ___.",["the service was late","the service was exactly on time","the speaker wants a sapphire"],"the service was late","The literal praise masks criticism.","meaning"),Q("sarcasm.q2","sarcasm.s2","context","A colleague known for sarcasm often ___.",["makes mocking remarks","speaks only in technical measurements","serves food on trays"],"makes mocking remarks","This is the habit sense.","context"),Q("sarcasm.q3","sarcasm.s1","register","Sarcasm can be risky at work because it may ___.",["sound mocking or be misunderstood","always function as a formal apology","describe a sanitation system"],"sound mocking or be misunderstood","The listener may take the words literally or feel mocked.","register"),Q("sarcasm.q4","sarcasm.s1","meaning","Which statement is sarcastic after a printer breaks?",["“That printer is a model of reliability,” said while it jams again.","“The printer is broken,” said plainly.","“I will call the technician,” said sincerely."],"“That printer is a model of reliability,” said while it jams again.","The literal compliment contradicts the obvious failure.","meaning")]});
D("sarcastic",{etymology:E("From sarcasm + -ic, via Greek sarkastikos, from sarkazein ‘speak bitterly’; the adjective describes mocking or falsely praising words.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sarcastic"),contexts:[C("sarcastic.s1","對話","His sarcastic comment about the empty coffee pot made the tired staff laugh despite the early meeting.","他对空咖啡壶的讽刺让疲惫的员工在一早的会议上笑了出来。","Sarcastic describes sharp words that mock someone or a situation.","About identifies the target of the comment; despite contrasts the mood.","The remark mocks the empty pot and the staff's need for coffee.") ,C("sarcastic.s2","對話","“Brilliant work,” she said sarcastically after he deleted the only backup copy.","他删掉唯一的备份后，她讽刺地说：“干得漂亮。”","Sarcastic can describe false praise used to express the opposite meaning.","After gives the action prompting the ironic praise.","The words praise, but the intended meaning is criticism.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","She was sarcastic when she sincerely thanked the careful technician and meant exactly what she said.","She was appreciative when she sincerely thanked the careful technician and meant exactly what she said.","Sarcastic implies mockery or opposite intent; sincere literal thanks are not sarcastic.")],quiz:[Q("sarcastic.q1","sarcastic.s1","meaning","A sarcastic remark is usually ___.",["mocking or cutting","a neutral measurement","a type of bread"],"mocking or cutting","The adjective describes words used to mock.","meaning"),Q("sarcastic.q2","sarcastic.s2","context","Someone says “Excellent job” after a clear mistake in a sarcastic tone. The praise is ___.",["false and meant as criticism","sincere and literal","a serving dish"],"false and meant as criticism","The second sense is false praise to express the opposite.","context"),Q("sarcastic.q3","sarcastic.s1","word-formation","Sarcastic is the adjective related to the noun ___.",["sarcasm","sardine","sapphire"],"sarcasm","The adjective is formed from the noun sarcasm.","word-formation"),Q("sarcastic.q4","sarcastic.s2","meaning","Which line is sarcastic after a computer crashes?",["“What a reliable machine,” said with an eye-roll.","“The screen is black,” said neutrally.","“I will restart it,” said sincerely."],"“What a reliable machine,” said with an eye-roll.","The praise means the opposite because of the failure.","meaning")]});
D("sardine",{etymology:E("From French sardine and Latin sardina, from Greek sardínē, a name for a small fish associated with Sardinia; modern English often means the fish sold fresh or canned.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sardine"),contexts:[C("sardine.s1","飲食","The cook mashed a canned sardine with lemon and parsley for the sandwiches.","厨师把一条罐头沙丁鱼和柠檬、欧芹一起捣碎，做成三明治馅料。","A sardine is a small oily sea fish, often sold fresh or in cans.","With lemon and parsley describes preparation; for the sandwiches gives its use.","The fish is used as food.")],mistakes:[M("plural","The shop received two sardine in each tin for the lunch order.","The shop received two sardines in each tin for the lunch order.","Two requires the plural form sardines.")],quiz:[Q("sardine.q1","sardine.s1","meaning","A sardine is a ___.",["small oily sea fish","young tree","blue precious stone"],"small oily sea fish","This is the fish sense.","meaning"),Q("sardine.q2","sardine.s1","context","A sardine sandwich is likely filled with ___.",["small fish, often canned","a serving tray","sandstone grains"],"small fish, often canned","Sardines are commonly eaten fresh or canned.","context"),Q("sardine.q3","sardine.s1","plural","One sardine, two ____.",["sardines","sardine's","sardine"],"sardines","The regular plural adds -s.","plural"),Q("sardine.q4","sardine.s1","meaning","Which food is made with a sardine?",["A small oily fish from the sea","A piece of carved sandstone","A blue corundum gem"],"A small oily fish from the sea","The noun names the sea fish.","meaning")]});
D("sardonic",{etymology:E("From French sardonique and Greek sardonios, an old term for a bitter or scornful laugh; the deeper origin is uncertain.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/sardonic"),contexts:[C("sardonic.s1","表情","A sardonic smile crossed her face when the official promised the third “final” deadline of the month.","官员承诺本月第三个“最后”期限时，她脸上掠过一丝讥讽的笑。","Sardonic can describe a smile showing bitter scorn.","When gives the trigger; quoted final signals the repeated empty promise.","The smile communicates contempt rather than amusement.") ,C("sardonic.s2","文學","The novel uses sardonic humor to criticize the officials who congratulate themselves for fixing a problem they caused.","小说用讽刺性的黑色幽默批评那些为解决自己制造的问题而自我庆祝的官员。","Sardonic can describe dark humor used to criticize people or things.","Who-clause identifies the target of the criticism.","The humor is bitter and critical.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The warm, sincere smile of gratitude was sardonic because it expressed no scorn or criticism.","The bitter, scornful smile after the empty promise was sardonic.","Sardonic means bitterly scornful; sincere gratitude is not scornful.")],quiz:[Q("sardonic.q1","sardonic.s1","meaning","A sardonic smile usually expresses ___.",["bitter scorn","pure gratitude","a salty taste"],"bitter scorn","The adjective often describes a scornful expression.","meaning"),Q("sardonic.q2","sardonic.s2","context","A writer uses sardonic humor to ___.",["criticize with dark, bitter wit","offer a literal medical diagnosis","describe a small fish"],"criticize with dark, bitter wit","This is the dark-humor sense.","context"),Q("sardonic.q3","sardonic.s1","confusable","Which expression is sardonic?",["A scornful smile at an obviously false promise","A warm smile of sincere thanks","A neutral smile for a photograph"],"A scornful smile at an obviously false promise","Sardonic conveys contempt or bitter irony.","confusable"),Q("sardonic.q4","sardonic.s2","meaning","The review's sardonic joke about the failed plan is intended to ___.",["criticize the plan with bitter humor","praise it without irony","describe the taste of canned fish"],"criticize the plan with bitter humor","Sardonic humor carries a critical, scornful edge.","meaning")]});
